; xfail: unknown identifier: LIMIT
; Reading a module global that is planned LATER (here: defined later in
; the file; the in-tree case was Page.scaly reading root_pages'
; BITMAP_ALL_FREE — a later-planned module) used to DROP the enclosing
; statement silently: the name fell through to a bare Type operand, the
; emitter emitted null for it, and the whole comparison vanished. It is
; a hard "unknown identifier" diagnostic now (collapse_operand_sequence
; binary loop). A pre-pass that planned all globals up front was tried
; and reverted — plan results not returned into the plan tree dangle.

function limit_matches(x: u64) returns bool
{
    if x = LIMIT
        return true
    false
}

define LIMIT u64 0x7FFFFFFFFFFFFFFF

if limit_matches(5 as u64)
    print "boom\n"
print "done\n"
